.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Provides a multi‑branch delegate dispatcher driven by a switch‑condition\&. 

\fBSwitchDelegate<TS, T>\fP extends the concept of \fRIFDelegate<T>\fP by supporting an arbitrary number of conditional branches\&. Each branch is identified by a case key of type \fITS\fP  and holds its own delegate chain\&. 

.PP
When \fBInvoke\fP is called, the condition function selects the active case, and the corresponding delegate chain is executed\&. If no delegate is registered for the selected case, nothing is invoked\&. 

.PP
This type is useful for state‑based dispatching, multi‑mode processing, or any scenario where behavior depends on a discrete selector rather than a boolean condition\&. 

.PP
\fBTemplate Parameters\fP
.RS 4
\fITS\fP The switch key type used to identify delegate branches\&. Must be non‑nullable\&. 
.br
\fIT\fP The argument type passed to subscribed delegates\&. 
.RE
.PP

